      "final_text": "Done \u2014 `check_candidate` returns `VERIFIED` on all 8 requirements, and `verify_passport` reproduces it.\n\n**The fix** (in [candidate/Solution.lean](<workspace>/candidate/Solution.lean)): the deployed Proposal 62 code credited an account with no recorded index from 0 whenever the market index was *strictly above* `compInitialIndex`. After the upgrade set a never-rewarded market's index to exactly `compInitialIndex`, borrowers were paid their full balance as COMP. The implementation now computes each hook in closed form with the spec's own `accrueSide`/`accrualStart`/`creditFor`/`grant` \u2014 i.e. start at `compInitialIndex` once the index has *reached* it (`\u2265`, the Proposal 64 rule) \u2014 with `none` exactly on the spec's revert conditions.\n\n**The proofs**: the five effect/success requirements follow by case analysis on those preconditions. The three global bounds go through the vendored `ProofForgeFin.Accumulator.Market` theory: each `exec` operation is mapped to a market action (`exec_act`: settles, transfers, payments, retunes, time passage), the upgrade state satisfies the invariant and potential bounds (`start_inv`, `start_pot`, `start_potOf` via `reinit`), and the library's `rewards_bounded`, `account_rewards_bounded`, and `rewards_after_no_position_bounded` give the three requirements.\n\n**Verification**: all 8 theorems accepted by all six kernels with only permitted axioms; property tests pass (2001 cases, no violations). Passport: [.proofforge/passport-001.json](<workspace>/.proofforge/passport-001.json), `passport_sha256 85e02fe499378ac7352bef241a50c6ffe66556151c86f24e1769ec93d7a81669`.",
